- Family and friend gatherings that can last all day and into the evening (yozakura = night blossom viewing)
- Company parties where junior employees are sent ahead to "reserve" prime spots at dawn

The philosophical heart of hanami is mono no aware—the bittersweet appreciation of transience. Cherry blossoms are most beautiful precisely because they fall. A single pink petal floating in a breeze is a meditation on the beauty of things that don't last.

Best spots: Ueno Park (Tokyo), Maruyama Park (Kyoto), Hirosaki Castle (Aomori), and the countless rivers and mountains throughout Japan.''',
