      description: '''Shinto is Japan's indigenous religion—not a set of doctrines, but a way of perceiving the sacred in nature. Kami (spirits or divine forces) inhabit everything: mountains, rivers, trees, rocks, and even exceptional humans after death.

Shinto has no founder, no sacred text, and no concept of sin. Instead, it focuses on maintaining harmony (wa) and purity (harae). Pollution (kegare)—physical or spiritual dirt—disrupts this harmony and must be cleansed through rituals.

