    CultureContent(
      id: 'japanese_islands_01',
      videoUrl: 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Qo7X9ATqa64',
      categoryId: 'region',
      title: 'Japan\'s Island Diversity: 6,852 Islands',
      subtitle: 'From sub-tropical Ishigaki to frigid Rebun—Japan is an archipelago',
      description: '''Japan consists of 6,852 islands stretching 3,000 km from sub-Arctic Hokkaido to sub-tropical Okinawa—an astonishing range of climates, cultures, and ecosystems within one nation.

The four main islands:
- **Honshu**: The main island; home to Tokyo, Kyoto, Osaka; Japan's political and cultural center
- **Hokkaido**: Sub-arctic north; vast wilderness, Ainu heritage, powder snow, dairy farming
- **Shikoku**: The "four provinces" island; famous for the 88-temple pilgrimage (Ohenro) walked by Buddhist pilgrims following the footsteps of the monk Kukai
- **Kyushu**: Southwestern island; volcanic, warm, historically Japan's gateway to Asia

Remote and extraordinary islands:

**Yakushima** (Kagoshima): A UNESCO World Heritage mountainous island covered in ancient cedar (yakusugi) forests—trees over 1,000 years old are common; Jomon Sugi is estimated to be between 2,000 and 7,000 years old (the minimum of ~2,200 years is scientifically confirmed; the upper estimate is disputed). Said to have inspired the forest in Miyazaki's "Princess Mononoke."

**Iriomote** (Okinawa): Japan's last true jungle; 90% uninhabited, home to the endemic Iriomote wildcat (only ~100 remain), mangrove rivers, and coral reefs.

**Naoshima** (Kagawa): A tiny island in the Seto Inland Sea transformed into a contemporary art destination—Benesse Art Site houses permanent installations by James Turrell, Yayoi Kusama, and Lee Ufan.

**Sado** (Niigata): Historically a place of exile for nobles and criminals; now famous for taiko drumming (Kodo), gold mines, and ibis conservation.

Island-hopping by ferry is one of Japan's most rewarding but underused travel experiences.''',
      imageUrl: 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1480796927426-f609979314bd?w=800',
      tags: ['islands', 'yakushima', 'naoshima', 'diversity', 'archipelago'],
      level: 2,
      createdAt: DateTime(2026, 5, 31),
      readTime: 6,
      sourceUrl: 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japan',
    ),

